#====================================================================
# Draft: petsc-complex 3.25.4 - PETSc's bundled f2cblaslapack already
#        ships the complex (z) BLAS/LAPACK routines, so a complex build
#        needs no OpenBLAS/MKL provider; and PETSC_USE_COMPLEX reaches
#        consumers through the installed petscconf.h, so the ABI macro
#        never has to be injected by the recipe to be correct
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-PETSC-COMPLEX-3254-SELF-CONTAINED-COMPLEX-BLAS
trigger_tool:           configure|make|conan
phase:                  configuration|dependency-resolution|packaging
error_signature:        download-f2cblaslapack|zgemm|zdotc|zheev|PETSC_USE_COMPLEX not defined|undefined reference to `zgemm_|no BLAS provider|self-contained BLAS

severity:               2
category:               conan-recipe-dependencies
match_keywords:         petsc, petsc-complex, 3.25.4, f2cblaslapack, 3.8.0.q2, zgemm, zdotc, zheev, complex BLAS, complex LAPACK, openblas, mkl, self-contained, PETSC_USE_COMPLEX, petscconf.h, petscsys.h, ABI consistency, --with-mpi=0, MPIUNI

title:                  A complex PETSc build stays fully self-contained by reusing the bundled f2cblaslapack (its z-routines are already f2c'd in), and PETSC_USE_COMPLEX propagates to consumers through the installed petscconf.h rather than through recipe -D flags

root_cause:             The instinct when moving from real to complex scalars is that a complex build now needs a real BLAS/LAPACK provider carrying zgemm/zdotc/zheev - normally OpenBLAS or MKL - which would drag an unpublished dependency into the OHOS graph. That is unnecessary for PETSc: configure's --download-f2cblaslapack=1 fetches f2cblaslapack-3.8.0.q2, a netlib f2c port that already contains blas/zgemm.c, blas/zdotc.c and lapack/zheev.c alongside the real routines. The second half of the problem is ABI visibility: it looks like consumers must be told the variant via -D PETSC_USE_COMPLEX, but PETSc generates the macro into the installed petscconf.h and petscsys.h includes it, so the header path already carries the correct ABI and a recipe that "helpfully" defines it is only duplicating an existing guarantee.
affected_scope:         Any PETSc configure in a self-contained/native recipe (the repo's petsc 3.25.x family), and more generally any project that offers a bundled BLAS/LAPACK fallback: check whether the bundled copy already covers the scalar variant before adding an external provider dependency. The petscconf.h propagation point applies to any project that generates a configured header consumed transitively by its umbrella header.
verification_cmd:       tar -tzf f2cblaslapack-3.8.0.q2.tar.gz | grep -E 'blas/zgemm\.c|blas/zdotc\.c|lapack/zheev\.c' && conan create archives/p/petsc-complex/3.25.4 -pr:h=ohos-aarch64 -pr:b=ohos-aarch64 --build=missing -nr

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           reuse-bundled-f2cblaslapack-plus-header-borne-abi-macro
rec_description:        Keep the same self-contained configure as the real-scalar sibling: --with-fc=0 --with-mpi=0 --download-f2cblaslapack=1, adding only --with-scalar-type=complex --with-precision=double. No requires() entry for BLAS/LAPACK and no external provider in the graph. Before assuming otherwise, verify the bundled mirror really covers the variant - for f2cblaslapack-3.8.0.q2 the complex routines are present (blas/zgemm.c, blas/zdotc.c, lapack/zheev.c), which is what makes the self-contained claim true rather than lucky. On the consumer side, do NOT rely on the recipe's cpp_info.defines to establish the ABI: PETSC generates PETSC_USE_COMPLEX into <prefix>/include/petscconf.h and petscsys.h (pulled in by petsc.h) includes it, so any consumer compiling against the installed headers gets the variant ABI automatically. Keep the defines in package_info() only so the generated CMake/pkg-config files are self-describing; treat the header as the source of truth. package() must still install the generated petscconf.h (i.e. use PETSc's own `make install`, do not hand-copy include/), otherwise consumers lose both the macro and the config values. Also keep package_type="library" with libs ["petsc","f2clapack","f2cblas"] and system_libs ["m","stdc++"] on Linux/OHOS.
rec_command:            conan create archives/p/petsc-complex/3.25.4 -pr:h=ohos-aarch64 -pr:b=ohos-aarch64 --build=missing -nr
rec_auto_fix:           false
